<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cabeço das Fráguas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cabeço das Fráguas is a hill in the district of Guarda in central Portugal, crowned by an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort. A rock inscription near its summit, written in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> alphabet around the turn of the eras, is one of the few known texts in the Lusitanian language. It records offerings of animals to local deities, perhaps in a ritual resembling the Roman suovetaurilia.</p></div>
